<div class="key-takeaways"><h2>Key takeaways</h2><ul>
<li>NOAA's Storm Events Database lists 180 hail reports for Hays County from 1967 to 2026.</li>
<li>San Marcos hail season peaks in spring: May (67 reports), April (57), and March (23) account for about 82% of all reports.</li>
<li>58 reports were golf-ball size (1.75 inches) or larger, and 8 were baseball size (2.75 inches) or larger.</li>
<li>The biggest stone on record, 4.5 inches, fell just north of San Marcos on March 16, 2000.</li>
<li>May 9, 2024 brought 3-inch hail west of the city and 70 mph gusts; 2024 had more Hays County hail reports (15) than any other year in the record.</li>
<li>Storm data supports a date of loss, but your claim still rests on documented roof damage and your policy terms.</li>
