<p>Older entries, such as 3-inch hail in 1967 and 1971, are listed only at the county level, so we cannot say exactly where they fell. The 2000 and 2006 events, by contrast, are pinned to the San Marcos area and describe damage many longtime residents still remember.</p>

<h3>May 9, 2024: hail and wind across Hays County</h3>

<p>The May 9, 2024 storms are the most significant recent hail event for San Marcos. NCEI lists <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=1181388" target="_blank" rel="noopener">3-inch hail at San Marcos Academy</a> west of the city, <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=1181409" target="_blank" rel="noopener">2.5-inch hail near the outlet mall</a>, <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=1181367" target="_blank" rel="noopener">2.5-inch hail near Wimberley</a>, <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=1181340" target="_blank" rel="noopener">baseball-size hail near Henly</a>, and <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=1181349" target="_blank" rel="noopener">3-inch hail south of Dripping Springs</a>.</p>

<p>The hail came with wind. NCEI records estimated 70 mph gusts that <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=1181424" target="_blank" rel="noopener">dropped a Chinese elm onto a building roof northwest of San Marcos</a> and <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=1181414" target="_blank" rel="noopener">damaged a church roof in the city</a>. The Hays County Judge signed a local disaster declaration afterward. That was a county declaration, not a federal one. The later federal declaration for spring 2024 storms, <a href="https://www.fema.gov/disaster/4781" target="_blank" rel="noopener">FEMA DR-4781</a>, included Hays County for Public Assistance only, which helps governments rather than individual homeowners. For most property owners, recovery from that storm ran through their own insurance policies.</p>

<h3>May 22, 2025: baseball hail east of I-35</h3>

<p>A year later, storms on May 22, 2025 produced baseball-size hail in Uhland and tennis-ball-size hail in Kyle, according to NCEI. Both areas are full of newer subdivisions with composition shingle roofs, and both are a short drive from San Marcos. If you live in Kyle, our <a href="/service-areas/kyle/">Kyle service area page</a> has more local detail.</p>

